---
source: tests/cli.rs
expression: "String::from_utf8_lossy(&output.stdout)"
---
Panes and the agents in them

Usage: multiplexer-driver pane [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  list       List every pane, shells included
  spawn      Open a new tab running a command
  split      Split a pane and run a command in the new one
  read       Read the last lines of a pane
  prompt     Type text into a pane and press Enter
  rename     Set a pane's label. The handle does not change
  interrupt  Send Ctrl-C to a pane
  kill       Close one pane, never its tab or workspace
  status     Report the agent status of a pane
  wait       Wait until a pane reaches a status
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --harness <HARNESS>
          Harness to drive. Required for workspace, pane, and raw

          Possible values:
          - tmux:  tmux
          - herdr: Herdr
          
          [env: MULTIPLEXER_DRIVER_HARNESS=]

      --session <SESSION>
          Harness server to use: a Herdr session name or a tmux -L socket name. Unset uses the ambient server
          
          [env: MULTIPLEXER_DRIVER_SESSION=]

      --pretty
          Indent single-object output. Lists stay JSON Lines

      --log-level <LOG_LEVEL>
          Diagnostics level on stderr: debug, info, warn, or error
          
          [env: RUST_LOG=]
          [default: warn]

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
